WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.771
Hunting for a job the traditional way is a lot of work.

00:00:06.771 --> 00:00:11.983
You keep track of a dozen job boards, and check each one by hand, every day.

00:00:11.983 --> 00:00:17.331
You end up with forty tabs open, and a spreadsheet that is always out of date.

00:00:17.331 --> 00:00:21.239
Then you type the same application form, again and again.

00:00:21.239 --> 00:00:23.502
jobwatch does that grind for you.

00:00:23.502 --> 00:00:24.325
Here is how.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.535
Your job hunt shouldn't be a full-time job.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:33.191
Every morning, Today opens on your own filters: a fit score of eighty or more,

00:00:33.191 --> 00:00:35.472
out of a hundred, and a pay floor.

00:00:35.472 --> 00:00:40.435
Jobs with no score or no pay listed wait at the end, or you can hide them.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.836
A job with no pay figure says so: pay unknown.

00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:50.575
You're never guessing.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.991
Queue the ones worth applying to.

00:00:54.991 --> 00:00:58.945
The queue is your short list, with the warnings to check first.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.349
On the company's own form,

00:01:02.349 --> 00:01:06.949
the extension fills what it can from your details and earlier answers.

00:01:06.949 --> 00:01:09.840
You check every field, and you press Submit.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:18.091
On a LinkedIn list, it counts how many of those jobs jobwatch already found.

00:01:18.091 --> 00:01:22.045
Read the same list again, and it tells you there's nothing new.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.330
Then track every application: its stage, the next step, and when to follow up.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.910
Before a call, open the prep sheet.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.680
And compare your real options side by side.
